ather than tracking `body_entered`/`exited`, so a block that melts on the pad can't leave it stuck. A child `StaticBody2D` pedestal (layer 2, joins `"water_solid"`, deliberately not `"ground"`/`"catwalk"` so it can't be ledge-grabbed) has a collider whose top follows the middle of the art's oval per frame (`SURFACE_TOP_PX`), resized on a per-instance shape. Sounds `interactive/button_press`/`interactive/button_release` follow `active`.
 - **Speed trap** (`res://scenes/interactive/speed_trap.gd` + `speed_trap.tscn`, `@tool`): a speed camera as a power **source** in the same contract as `Button` (`Area2D`, group `"power_source"`, `is_powered()`, `powered_changed(on)`, so a `PowerTarget` picks it in `sources` and a conductor wire attaches to it by adjacency). The node origin is the centre of a 16×16 tile (the cell a conductor files it under); the sensor strip is the vertical line at the origin's x, from that tile's bottom edge (the floor) up `strip_height` px (default 32), with a camera on a post beside it (`post_side`, left or right) and a three-digit screen. The `Area2D` has no layers and monitoring off; its `CollisionShape2D` (resized per instance from `strip_height`) only shows the strip in the editor, because a 600 px/s surf moves 10 px a frame and would step over a thin overlap. **Crossing**: each physics frame it takes the sign of the player's x relative to the line; a change of sign between two frames, with the player's collider overlapping the strip's height and a step of at most `MAX_CROSS_STEP` (48 px, so a teleport or respawn isn't a crossing), is a read, in either direction; standing in the strip does nothing, and a frame exactly on the line waits for the next. **Read**: `require_surfing` (default on) reads a surfing player only, through `get_surf_speed()` (the board's ground speed, or the horizontal speed it carries in the air), and ignores any other crossing entirely (no flash, no reading), so a pad launch or a swing release can't trigger it; with it off the reading is the player's `|velocity.x|`. A dead or dancing player is ignored. The reading is `floor(speed * display_scale)` (default 0.1, clamped to 999) and the pass test is `speed >= threshold_speed` (default 450): pick a threshold whose product with `display_scale` is whole, so a passing speed never displays below the limit. A pass powers the trap for `hold_time` seconds (default 5; 0 = latched until the level is reset), restarts